      "url": "https://ncac.org/banned-books-week/banned-books-top-10",
      "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"55f2a7d5b5396679\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe ALA Office for Intellectual Freedom tracked 377 challenges to library, school, and university materials and services in 2019. Of the 566 books challenged or banned in 2019, the following are the top 10 most frequently challenged: George by Alex Gino Reasons: challenged, banned, restricted, and hidden to avoid controversy; for LGBTQIA+ content and a transgender character; because schools and libraries should not “put books in a child’s hand that require discussion”; for sexual references; and for conflicting with a religious viewpoint and “traditional family structure”\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"55f2a7d5b5396679\">>>",
